# Data breakpoints: stop when a value changes, wherever it changes.
# Set a breakpoint on the first "yield" to get stopped, then remove it. In Variables,
# right-click a value and choose "Break on Value Change":
# - Registers, r15 (Stage). Continue: it stops after the line that changed it,
#   and the stop names that line.
# - Devices, d0 (heater), On. Only this script changes it.
# - Devices, d1 (sensor), Temperature. It changes between ticks (the "cold snap"
#   and "sunrise" events), so the stop names the event instead of a line.
# - Stack, 0 (top): the push at the start set it; the "put" in heat changes it.
# - Add Stage to Watch, then right-click it there: Watch expressions work too.
# Right-click a data breakpoint in the Breakpoints view, Edit Condition, to stop
# only on some changes (Stage == 2). Data breakpoints are kept for the next run.
alias Stage r15
alias Heater d0
alias Sensor d1
define Cold 280
define Warm 290
move Stage 0
push 0
loop:
l r0 Sensor Temperature
blt r0 Cold heat
bgt r0 Warm idle
yield
j loop
heat:
s Heater On 1
move Stage 1
put db 0 r0 # remember how cold it got
yield
j loop
idle:
s Heater On 0
move Stage 2
yield
j loop
